IO-46: route the groundwater flow read from a runoff interface file

In a USE RUNOFF run RunoffInterfaceFile::readResults() restores each
subcatchment's groundwater outflow into ctx.subcatches.gw_flow (cfs), but the
node inflow is built from the groundwater solver's per-unit-area rate
(groundwater_.state().gw_flow, interpolated from old_gw_rate_), which the file
path never set, so no groundwater reached the drainage system. After reading a
record, set the rate from the file's flow divided by the subcatchment area (the
old rate is already rolled at the top of the runoff loop).

The SAVE RUNOFF record was also written before the groundwater step (and
before washoff and the LID fold), so each record carried the previous runoff
step's groundwater flow. Write it after the groundwater step, where legacy
runoff_saveToFile() writes it; the records then match 5.3.0's.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-46_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 839529d..7896995 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
@@ -2137,6 +2137,17 @@ void SWMMEngine::stepRunoff(double dt_routing) noexcept {
                 new_runoff_ms_ = ctx_.options.totalDurationMs();
                 break;
             }
+            // The file holds each subcatchment's groundwater outflow in cfs;
+            // the node inflow interpolates the per-unit-area rate (legacy
+            // gw->newFlow), whose old value was rolled at the top of the loop.
+            for (int i = 0; i < ctx_.n_subcatches(); ++i) {
+                const auto ui = static_cast<std::size_t>(i);
+                if (ui >= groundwater_.state().gw_flow.size()) break;
+                const double a = ctx_.subcatches.area[ui]
+                               / ucf::UCF(ucf::LANDAREA, ctx_.options);
+                groundwater_.state().gw_flow[ui] =
+                    a > 0.0 ? ctx_.subcatches.gw_flow[ui] / a : 0.0;
+            }
             if (file_dt <= 0.0) file_dt = 1.0;
             new_runoff_time_ = old_runoff_time_ + file_dt;
             new_runoff_ms_ = new_runoff_ms_ + 1000.0 * file_dt;
@@ -2397,12 +2408,6 @@ void SWMMEngine::stepRunoff(double dt_routing) noexcept {
         // accumulating here would capture the pre-LID runoff and miss the LID
         // exchange, leaving the continuity unbalanced (issue #102 D/E).
 
-        // A4b'. Phase 1b auto-save hook — when the runoff interface file
-        // is open in SAVE mode, emit one record per substep. saveResults
-        // is a cheap no-op when the file is not in SAVE mode, so the
-        // unconditional call here costs nothing for ordinary runs.
-        saveRunoffIfaceStep(dt_runoff);
-
         // A4c. Surface quality: buildup + washoff. IGNORE_QUALITY skips all
         //      pollutant buildup/washoff/sweeping (legacy runoff.c:274
         //      `if (IgnoreQuality) continue;`).
@@ -2914,6 +2919,15 @@ void SWMMEngine::stepRunoff(double dt_routing) noexcept {
             stepGroundwater(dt_runoff);
         }
 
+        // A4b'. Phase 1b auto-save hook — when the runoff interface file
+        // is open in SAVE mode, emit one record per substep. saveResults
+        // is a cheap no-op when the file is not in SAVE mode, so the
+        // unconditional call here costs nothing for ordinary runs.
+        // Written after the washoff, LID and groundwater steps, as legacy
+        // runoff_saveToFile() runs at the end of runoff_execute(), so the
+        // record holds this step's GW flow and washoff, not the last step's.
+        saveRunoffIfaceStep(dt_runoff);
+
         // A6c. Accumulate runoff mass-balance totals now that the LID routing
         // has finalised subcatches.runoff (moved from A4b — see note there).
         accumulateRunoffMassBalance(dt_runoff);
